"""Stage 3 merge for report 59 (Tappsk)."""
import json
C = {x["id"]: x for x in json.load(open("Tools/prd_ledger/canonical.json"))}
def ext(cid, text):
    if text not in C[cid]["statement"]: C[cid]["statement"] += text
def add(cid, section, title, statement):
    if cid in C: return
    C[cid] = dict(id=cid, title=title, statement=statement, section=section, cards=[], reports=[], merged_from=[])

add("C276", "undecided", "An optional event time (and duration) on a task or habit, distinct from its reminder, with the day sorted by it and shown on the widget",
    "Report 59 (Tappsk, 15,176 reviews): the most persistent functional request across eight years — U_SCHEDULE_REQ 471 (3.10%, Very strong): REQ_TIME 186, REQ_SORT 132, REQ_CALENDAR_VIEW 118, REQ_ADVANCE_REMINDER 68; a task has a reminder time but no event time, so the day's list does not order itself by timeline ('чтобы задача на 09:00 стояла выше задачи на 11:00' — so the 09:00 task sits above the 11:00 task) and users write the time into the title ('тк нет в приложении времени - я просто в названиях пишу время'); REQ_TIME is at its era maximum in E6 (1.8%) and is the third-largest 4★ theme (69 of 1,671) — the report's hypothesis is that it converts the most frequent 4★ request into 5★; the guard is bloat — PR_KEEP_SIMPLE 49 ask the developer not to change the app. Related: [[C050]] (to-dos alongside habits), [[C006]] (stay minimal), [[C053]] (time-of-day segments), [[C198]] (routine blocks).")

ext("C050", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the strongest evidence yet for the hybrid — a daily to-do list with a habit row on the same screen is what 15,176 reviewers praise: PR_ALLINONE 293 (1.93%), PR_HABITS 445, and the most-voted review in the corpus (156 votes) is 'Задачи и привычки в одном приложении - гениально' (tasks and habits in one app — genius); switchers come from Notes/Reminders, Todoist, Trello, Notion and Things. The to-do half brings its own design decisions: today / tomorrow / this week / later buckets (PR_SECTIONS 134, PR_ONE_SCREEN 82; Germany praises the one screen at 8.92×), automatic carry-over of unfinished tasks (PR_AUTO_CARRY 69 — 'all your unfinished today's tasks move to tomorrow') which the report says to keep as the default but with a per-task opt-out because recurring tasks carrying over is unwanted by 28 and recurring tasks invisible on future dates by 32; and the missing event time ([[C276]]).")
ext("C006", " Report 59 (Tappsk): PR_SIMPLE 1,704 (11.23%) — 'Ничего лишнего. Удобно' (nothing superfluous); 'the unneeded, obstructive options of the rivals are absent'; PR_KEEP_SIMPLE 49 explicitly ask the developer not to change it; the cost is NEG_LIMITED 115 (0.76%, 3.39★) who find it too basic, against NEG_BLOAT 5 — the trade is worth it at 15,176 reviews.")
ext("C264", " Report 59 (Tappsk): entry speed is a named reason for choosing the app — 'позволяет тебе записать задачу быстрее чем ты ее забудешь' (write the task down faster than you forget it); 'Задачи добавляются за пол секунды' (added in half a second); voice entry by holding the add button praised by 52.")
ext("C254", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the one-screen today / tomorrow / later layout with habits on top is the praised overview (PR_SECTIONS 134, PR_ONE_SCREEN 82, PR_SWIPE 58 reschedule by swipe; 'Die Ansicht „heutige und zukünftige Aufgaben“ ist bei keiner Anderen App so gut und Übersichtlich aufgeteilt').")
ext("C109", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the 7-day trial that charged immediately or on day six is the largest single source of 1★ reviews across eight years — MON_AUTO_CHARGE 229 (1.51%, mean 1.82★) carries 163 of the 674 1★ (24.2%), co-occurs with MON_TRIAL 111 and MON_REFUND 113; a year's fee (999 ₽ named 73 times) taken at once ('при выборе бесплатной недели сразу списали деньги за год'; '«7 дней бесплатно», а сами втихую списываете на 6 день' — you quietly charge on day 6), charges after deletion ('Списывают деньги, даже если приложение удалено'), peaked 2.9% of 2020 and still 1.2% of 2024–26; the fix list: no charge before day 7, a visible countdown, one-tap cancel inside the app, a confirmation e-mail with the renewal date; a card-required trial is itself a barrier ('полная версия в пробном периоде требует привязки карты').")
ext("C152", " Report 59 (Tappsk): a confirmation e-mail with the renewal date is the report's first immediate fix (MON_AUTO_CHARGE 229, MON_CANCEL_TROUBLE 73).")
ext("C163", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the 7-day trial converts to the annual (999 ₽) by default; 111 of 306 trial mentions report an immediate charge and the annual sum is what makes the 1★ ('a year's money').")
ext("C112", " Report 59 (Tappsk): MON_CANCEL_TROUBLE 73 (1.0% of the latest era, its peak) — the subscription is hard to find and cancel, and the direct-card route for Russian users has no cancellation at all because App Store subscription management no longer shows the app ('В Айфоне в подписках вас у меня нет' — you are not in my iPhone subscriptions, 1★); a cancellation that works without the App Store and stops retries after deletion is an immediate fix.")
ext("C210", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the one case where off-store billing was forced (App Store payments blocked for Russian users from 2022-03) shows the cost: the direct-card route is praised by those who wanted to pay (54 of 74 payment-route reviews are 5★) but produces charges after deletion and a subscription the phone cannot show or cancel ('После отмены подписки приложение каждый раз пытается списать с карты средства' — after cancelling, the app keeps trying to charge the card) — if an off-store route is unavoidable, it needs in-app cancellation and bounded retries ([[C232]]).")
ext("C029", " Report 59 (Tappsk): U_BILLING 485 (3.20%, mean 2.30★) is the largest negative that is neither a price objection nor a product defect; even the reviewer's own missed cancellation ('забыла отменить подписку', 5★) lands as a support ticket in the reviews, and refunds are reported both granted ('Все вернули! Оперативно') and refused ('Деньги, естественно, никто не возвращает').")
ext("C221", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 'списали деньги за приложение, которого у меня нет' (money taken for an app I no longer have) — without a receipt naming the product, a renewal on a deleted app reads as fraud.")
ext("C104", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the January-2021 update capped the free tier at 20 tasks (reviewers also report 10, 3 and '2 habits, 2 recurring'), removed free habits for some ('раньше можно было использовать две, а теперь НИ ОДНОЙ' — before two, now NONE) and simultaneously stopped recognising existing purchases — MON_FREE_CUT 103 (80 in 2021-01→04), BUG_PURCHASE 57 in the era (its peak), any price objection 10.1% of the era (its peak), churn 2.2% (peak), the lowest era mean after launch (4.50★), the second most-voted review in the corpus (94 votes); the developer's reply ('it is 50') did not match the app ('only 20 are available').")
ext("C191", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the 2021-01 cut shrank free capacity users had already filled — habits removed from the free tier for existing users and a 20-task cap on lists people were using; 2021-01 was the busiest month of the corpus (372 reviews) and 2021-03 the lowest-rated (4.19★).")
ext("C001", " Report 59 (Tappsk): free habits were removed for some users in the 2021-01 cut and the 20-task cap was later lifted again — reviewers name 2, 3, 5, 10, 20 and 50 as the free cap in different months, and the report could not establish the cap at any date; a moving boundary is itself a grievance (MON_DISCLOSURE 80).")
ext("C186", " Report 59 (Tappsk): lifetime buyers are the ones asked to pay again — BUG_PURCHASE 45 and MON_PAID_TWICE 28 of the 430 lifetime reviews; 57 lifetime reviews are 1–2★; the 2021-01 update is the largest cluster and the rest spread to 2026: 'Покупала версию «Навсегда», спустя год написали, что пора опять оплатить «навсегда» ещё раз' (bought Forever; a year later told it was time to pay forever again); 'Купила навсегда, а получается не навсегда'.")
ext("C033", " Report 59 (Tappsk): BUG_PURCHASE 142 (0.94%, 2.81★, 8.43× among purchasers) — 'оплачено 990руб за подписку, но работать в этой программе нельзя пока ещё 1499 руб не заплатите' (990 ₽ paid but you cannot work until you pay another 1,499 ₽); a lifetime unlock listed in the phone's subscriptions as 'for a year'; the fix: restore the lifetime unlock from any receipt, on any device, on the Mac, after a reinstall, with no annual charge in between.")
ext("C127", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 'never show the lifetime buyer a subscription paywall' is an immediate fix — an app that sells lifetime, annual and monthly SKUs plus a 7-day trial side by side let a subscription charge reach lifetime owners ('купил полную версию на всегда за 1500 тыс, сегодня списалось 999 рублей за подписку' — bought forever for 1,500; today 999 ₽ taken for a subscription); lifetime buyers carry the highest problem lifts among purchasers (MON_PAID_TWICE 8.89×, BUG_PURCHASE 8.43×, SUP_NONE 6.09×) even though the one-time option is praised 93 times against 23 subscription objections.")
ext("C065", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 147 of 1,090 purchasers (13.5%) rate 1–2★; among purchasers BUG_PURCHASE lifts 8.43×, MON_PAID_TWICE 8.89×, SUP_NONE 6.09×, BUG_SYNC 5.71×, NEG_DEV_PROMISE 4.43× — the paid segment concentrates every failure class; 'написано, что поддерживается семейный доступ' (it says Family Sharing is supported) is a paid-twice complaint.")
ext("C003", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the lifetime unlock is the monetization asset of a 15,176-review app — 396 of 1,090 stated purchases name it (36.3% of purchasers, 12.82× lift), MON_ONETIME_PRAISE 93 against MON_SUBSCRIPTION objections 23 ('the reverse of most habit apps'), MON_VALUE 465 at 4.93★ ('спасибо разработчикам за отсутсвие подписки'; '5€ de por vida que es lo que te cobran las demás al mes' — €5 for life, what the others charge per month); Germany praises the one-time option at 2.95×; the seasonal discount is what sells it (MON_DISCOUNT 129 of purchasers, 8.02× — 'дождался скидку и купил премиум навсегда'; an offer popped up 'с хорошей скидкой, не задумываясь взял') and the free cap barely does (13 purchasers cite it); buying to support the developer is a stated trigger (MON_DONATE_WISH 18).")
ext("C113", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the discount that sells the lifetime unlock also generates disclosure complaints — 'Kurz nach dem Kauf wurde der Preis durch einen Zufallsgenerator reduziert' (shortly after the purchase the price was reduced by a random generator); the same lifetime named at 449 ₽ and 2,500 ₽ within a year; offers that vanish ('Предложение куда-то исчезло и желание купить пропало') and a buy button that is inactive; the report's fix: one price per region and no re-pricing within days of a purchase — a predictable seasonal sale rather than random rotation reconciles the two findings ([[C003]]).")
ext("C061", " Report 59 (Tappsk): PR_FREE 493 (3.25%, 4.91★ — 'no limit on the to-do list in the free version'), PR_NO_ADS 127, and buying 'чтобы поддержать разработчиков' (to support the developers) / 'чтобы отблагодарить разработчиков' (to thank the developers) as stated purchase triggers; the report says keep a free tier genuinely usable for tasks.")
ext("C097", " Report 59 (Tappsk): MON_DONATE_WISH 18 — reviewers buy the lifetime unlock explicitly to support or thank the developer.")
ext("C147", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 40 purchasers bought within days because the app worked in the first days ('Поюзал один день и купил навсегда' — used it one day and bought forever; 'took premium the same day I downloaded it').")
ext("C007", " Report 59 (Tappsk): a 2-habit / 2-recurring free cap is the most frequent objection in every era — MON_FREE_LIMIT 697 (4.59%, Very strong, 3.82★), the top 3★ theme (80 of 481), third in 4★ (247), and 'great app, but only two habits free' is the typical 4★ (praise + price objection share 601 reviews); 'two habits is too few to evaluate' ('неинтересно так пробовать'; '2 alışkanlıktan fazlasına premium istiyor', the most-voted Turkish review); the report's experiment is raising the cap to three (reviewers propose three or five) and stating the caps on the listing, predicting fewer 1–3★ with no loss of lifetime purchases because purchases are driven by discounts, not the cap (13 of 1,090 purchasers cite it); SA, TR, SE and ES over-index on the cap complaint.")
ext("C222", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the cap held at 2 habits for five years generates a steady 4.4–5.1% objection per era with no sign of decay; three is the number reviewers repeatedly propose as enough to evaluate.")
ext("C133", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the quantity gate (2 habits, 2 recurring tasks, a few reminders) is the top objection at 697 reviews while the capability gates (iCloud sync, Mac) draw a fraction of that.")
ext("C218", " Report 59 (Tappsk): MON_DISCLOSURE 80 (1.95★) and MON_PAYWALL_SURPRISE 64 (1.70★) — 'Пишите сразу, что ПО платное, а не встроенные покупки' (say up front that the software is paid, not 'in-app purchases'); 50 + 44 of the 674 1★; the listing does not state the caps and the report's experiment is to state them.")
ext("C110", " Report 59 (Tappsk): paywall surprise 64 at 1.70★ — the lowest-rated monetization code — from users who thought the app was free.")
ext("C093", " Report 59 (Tappsk): MON_UPSELL 97 (0.64%, 3.33★) — 'Каждый день по 30 раз пихают мне всплывающее окошко «Купите нашу полную версию»' (thirty times a day the buy-our-full-version pop-up); Germany reports it at 2.36×, purchasers at 2.44×.")
ext("C026", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the largest documented case — App Store payment became unavailable to Russian users from 2022-03; MON_PAYMENT_METHOD 74 (72 on the ru storefront, 54 of them 5★ because the reviewers want to pay and ask how — 'не могу оплатить премиум - версию, с кем мне связаться'; 'Вы теряете живые деньги' — you are losing real money); support arranged card or carrier billing case by case within minutes ('в течении 10-20 минут решили'; 'у меня мобильный оператор Megafon') and from 2024 a direct bank-card route is praised ('спасибо, что можно оплачивать напрямую по банковской карте'; 'за возможность альтернативной оплаты подписки для РФ'); the same era brought switchers from Trello and Notion after those services left Russia; the cost is the cancellation gap ([[C210]], [[C112]]). Removing the Russian storefront drops payment-access complaints from 0.7% to 0.0% and billing from 3.2% to 1.4%.")
ext("C231", " Report 59 (Tappsk): monetisation pain is geographic and product love is not — without the Russian storefront praise (76.8%), ease and the free-limit objection are unchanged while billing falls 3.2% → 1.4% and payment access 0.7% → 0.0%; billing 3.7% in Russian-speaking storefronts vs 1.0% in English-speaking; high-star reviews hide support tickets (CONTRA_RATING 155: 102 are 4–5★ reviews whose text reports a crash, charge or refund request — 'Возможно ли вернуть деньги после списания', 5★), so star-filtered monitoring misses refund requests.")
ext("C062", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the English-speaking group (us, gb, ca, au, in: 725 reviews) and Latin America (br + mx: 639) describe outcomes at about twice the global rate (20.3% / 21.3% vs 9.6%) with billing at 1.0% / 0.8% vs 3.7% Russian-speaking; Brazil is the growth market of the late corpus (32.1% of its reviews in the latest era, lowest 1–2★ share above 500 reviews); continental Europe carries the highest price objection (10.6%) and SA + TR 13.6%; no market uniquely asks for a desktop.")
ext("C027", " Report 59 (Tappsk): Ukraine is the only storefront where a language request is distinctive — REQ_LANG 8 (7.75×) ask for a Ukrainian interface, which the 17-language listing does not declare (nor Kazakh); Russian is written from 46 storefronts including 59 reviews on the US storefront; BUG_TRANSLATION 7 (a German widget in Russian).")
ext("C031", " Report 59 (Tappsk): four dated regression clusters in three years — 2021-10-22→25 an iOS-15-era update left iPhone 6/6+/7 on iOS 12–14 unable to open the app (33 crash reports in four days); 2023-06→10 completing a recurring task closed the app (trigger isolated by a reviewer to the 'show completed tasks' setting, build 2.5.397 named, 'no progress on this bug in three months'); 2023-08→12 the calendar opened on the same month of 2022; 2023-10 freezes after one action — the regression era carries the highest crash rate after launch (2.6%) and U_REGRESSION 296 'produced most of the product's 1–3★ reviews outside billing'; a launch-crash cluster in 2026-05; a locale-specific crash when setting a habit reminder appears almost only in Turkey (BUG_HABITS 19.99×, BUG_REMINDER 11.80×, BUG_CRASH 8.43×; 1–2★ 15.7% vs 5.9% global) with two Korean reports — test reminder flows under each locale.")
ext("C156", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the report's immediate fix is 'a release check on the oldest supported iOS and on the show-completed-tasks path before shipping; a fast hotfix path' — the 2021-10 crash hit only older iPhones and the 2023 crash only one setting path; the Turkish habit-reminder crash adds locale to the gate.")
ext("C175", " Report 59 (Tappsk): BUG_UPDATE 103 (2.83★) and the four release-clustered regressions ([[C031]]); the quietest release era (E4, 2022-03 → 2023-05) is also the best-rated (4.70★, praise 80.3%, defects 3.5%), and the regression era that followed the lowest since launch on crashes.")
ext("C040", " Report 59 (Tappsk): BUG_WIDGET 100 (0.66%) — widgets blank or stale after updates and not changing at day change ('при переключении дня задачи на виджете не меняются'; 'каждый раз обещают направить разработчикам, но проблема остается' — each time they promise to pass it on, the problem remains); fix: widgets that refresh at day change without opening the app; the 2.6.2 release notes list 'faster widgets'.")
ext("C039", " Report 59 (Tappsk): BUG_REMINDER 96 (0.63%, 2.78★) in every era — 'unless you open the app every other day, the reminders you set will stop working'; 'за весь день дай бог словить хотя бы 2 уведомления' (lucky to catch two notifications a day); PR_REMINDERS 401 shows the same feature is a top praise when it works.")
ext("C030", " Report 59 (Tappsk): BUG_SYNC 61 (5.71× among purchasers — sync is Premium-only) — 'На iphone не работает синхронизация'; the 2.6.2 release notes lead with 'iCloud sync more reliable'; a paid user lost everything and the account ('все записи удалились и больше не могу авторизоваться').")
ext("C034", " Report 59 (Tappsk): U_DATA_RISK 104 (0.69%) — 'но все мои задачи пропали' (all my tasks disappeared); 'Нигде не указано, что задачу надо обязательно сохранить' (nowhere does it say a task must be saved) — an unsaved-edit loss reads as data loss.")
ext("C013", " Report 59 (Tappsk): iCloud sync between devices is Premium and reviewers ask for it free ('в бесплатной версии синхронизировать устройства нельзя'; 'оставить синхронизацию в бесплатной версии'); the Mac app was sold separately in 2020–22 (MON_PER_DEVICE 59: 'Она платная для тех кто уже премиум?') and later folded into Premium.")
ext("C271", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the Mac app shipped 2020-06 and was sold separately from iPhone Premium — MON_PER_DEVICE 59 ('is it paid for those who already have premium?'), its peak 0.8% of that era; later reviewers describe Mac sync as part of Premium.")
ext("C251", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the Mac app was left behind — 'Там какое то старое приложение, которое давно не обновляется' (some old app that has not been updated in ages); 'garder à jour la version Mac qui semble délaissé' (keep the Mac version up to date, it seems abandoned) — and is the reason several leave for Things ('пришлось отказаться в пользу things из-за отсутствия поддержки Mac').")
ext("C044", " Report 59 (Tappsk): U_PLATFORM_REQ 385 (2.54%) — REQ_DESKTOP 208, REQ_WEB 104, REQ_ANDROID 28; desktop requests fall from 6.0% of the launch year to 0.6% after the Mac app and hold near 1% since, shifting to Windows and the browser ('Сделайте версию для ПК на WINDOWS 10'; 'нужна веб версия, товарищи'); the report's experiment is a read-mostly web view priced into Premium to test demand before a full client; REQ_WATCH fell from 4.7% to 0.0% after the Watch app shipped.")
ext("C022", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_WATCH 81 fell from 4.7% of the launch year to 0.0% of the latest era as PR_WATCH 37 appeared — a request that stops is the trace of a shipped feature.")
ext("C080", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_DARK (13) ends in 2021-10, consistent with a dark theme shipping; REQ_THEMES 70, REQ_ICON 20, REQ_FONT 21 continue.")
ext("C010", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_BACKFILL 62 (rising to 0.8% in the latest era) — unfinished tasks roll to today and cannot be marked done for the day they were done ('если я выполнила задачу в 00:01 и хочу отметить её выполненной за предыдущую дату' — did it at 00:01 and want to mark it for the previous date); the report's experiment: mark done for a past date.")
ext("C170", " Report 59 (Tappsk): NEG_DAY_BOUNDARY 19 — 'Как быть совам' (what about night owls, 1★); the report proposes a user-set day boundary alongside back-dating.")
ext("C256", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 'чтобы можно было задачу пометить как НЕ сделанную' (so a task can be marked as NOT done) — a missed item cannot be marked as missed, only carried forward.")
ext("C012", " Report 59 (Tappsk): habits show a week, not a month — 'Не нашел полноценную сводную статистику по всем привычкам' (no proper summary across all habits, 3★); REQ_STATS 114 (1.3% of the latest era); the experiment is a month view per habit.")
ext("C208", " Report 59 (Tappsk): U_ATTACH_REQ 223 (1.47%) — REQ_PHOTO 124, REQ_NOTES 106 ('ГДЕ ПРИКРЕПИТЬ ФОТО' — WHERE DO I ATTACH A PHOTO); one of the requests that never stops across eight years.")
ext("C071", " Report 59 (Tappsk): NEG_DEV_PROMISE 88 rising to 1.1% of the latest era, 4.43× among purchasers — 'there were added zero new features'; 'Два года прошу добавить эту простую фичу' (asking for this simple feature for two years, 1★); 'приложение вообще не меняется годами'; REQ_TIME, REQ_BACKFILL, REQ_PHOTO, REQ_STATS and REQ_SHARED never stop; SUP_NONE also peaks in the latest era (0.8%).")
ext("C196", " Report 59 (Tappsk): stagnation is the dominant criticism of the latest era — 'nothing changes' (NEG_DEV_PROMISE 1.1%) alongside subscriptions still being sold.")
ext("C094", " Report 59 (Tappsk): a guilt-trip dismiss button — 'пусть разработчики грустят' (let the developers be sad) — is named in 2.04% of reviews (REV_SOLICITED 309, mean 4.77★, 1.6–2.5% of every era from 2020-01, coinciding with a 10× volume jump); most reviewers quote it fondly ('adorei a estratégia para deixarmos a avaliação'), but 12 of 309 are 1–2★ about the prompt itself ('это манипуляция эмоциями' — emotional manipulation; 'Хватит меня каждую секунду просить оставить отзыв'; 'Saudumme Formulierung') and it feeds distrust of the other reviews (REV_DISTRUST 32: 'начитались купленных отзывов'); the report's experiment: keep the prompt, change the dismiss wording, suppress it after a purchase, a crash or a support ticket.")
ext("C150", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 'Хватит меня каждую секунду просить оставить отзыв' (stop asking me every second to leave a review, 1★) — cadence, not just timing.")
ext("C059", " Report 59 (Tappsk): PR_DEV 1,244 (8.20%, 4.96★, rising to 10.0% of the latest era) — reviewers thank the developer by name, praise fast Telegram replies ('Поддержка решила вопрос очень быстро'; 'j'ai réussi à joindre le support par Télégram qui a été d'une grande aide'; 'поддержка подарила мне подписку навсегда другой аккаунт'), and a fixed bug earns a 'P.S. Все исправлено, спасибо'; the report says keep the developer's visible presence.")
ext("C239", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the developer's own vc.ru article brought the first users (MKT_PRESS 13) and a Russian creator is itself praised ('это еще и русский создатель а не зарубежный').")
ext("C036", " Report 59 (Tappsk): reviewers praise Telegram and condemn e-mail — 'пишу на почту уже 2 раза, ответа нет' (e-mailed twice, no reply); 'На почту пишешь не отвечают, в тг пишешь бот' (e-mail unanswered; on Telegram you get a bot); SUP_NONE 64 (6.09× among purchasers), SUP_CONTACT 31, both more frequent in the latest eras; fix: route billing and sync tickets to the channel that answers and acknowledge bug reports with a status.")
ext("C215", " Report 59 (Tappsk): payment-route questions were answered 'within 10–20 minutes' in 2022 and earned 5★; billing e-mails that go unanswered earn 1★ — the same company, different channels.")
ext("C142", " Report 59 (Tappsk): NEG_UI_CONFUSING 152 (1.00%, rising to 1.4% in the latest era) — cannot find how to delete a habit or set a reminder on a habit ('не могу понять как удалить ненужную привычку').")
ext("C075", " Report 59 (Tappsk): NEG_ONBOARDING 78 (0.51%, 3.27★) — hidden gestures and an unexplained score make first use confusing even in an app praised for simplicity.")
ext("C217", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 'не очень понятно что значит 115' (not clear what 115 means) — the productivity score is unexplained on screen.")
ext("C157", " Report 59 (Tappsk): a daily productivity score with a trend arrow demotivates a minority — NEG_SCORE 23 vs PR_SCORE 84: 'ОЧЕНЬ ДЕМОТИВИРУЕТ эта стрелочка которая показывает насколько я продуктивна' (this arrow showing how productive I am is VERY demotivating, 4★).")
ext("C246", " Report 59 (Tappsk): PR_NO_ADS 127 (0.84%, 4.91★) with no ad complaint coded across 15,176 reviews; 'no ads in the free tier' is on the report's keep list.")
ext("C042", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 'As an ADHD person'; 'keeps me together with my bad ADHD'; 'Я очень забывчивая, и это приложение буквально спасает меня' (very forgetful; this app literally saves me) — OUT_MEMORY 326 (2.15%), USE_HEALTH distinctive in the US (6.89×) and UK (8.76×), OUT_MEMORY in France (3.34×) and Sweden (5.01×); these users are the most exposed to the missing task time; students (USE_STUDY 90 — 'made a student's life five times easier') and managers (USE_WORK 163 — 'the flow of tasks is endless') are the other named contexts.")
ext("C183", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the one-screen day plan with habits on top is what forgetful and ADHD reviewers credit ('keeps me together with my bad ADHD').")
ext("C005", " Report 59 (Tappsk): switchers to the app (COMP_SWITCHED_FROM 110, 4.87★) outnumber leavers to another app (CHURN_SWITCHED 43) — they come from Notes and Reminders ('Гораздо удобней стандартных заметок и напоминаний'), paper, Todoist, Trello and Notion (after those services left Russia) and Things ('Desinstalei o Things por causa desse app'); leavers name TickTick and Things, for the missing Mac support and task time; COMP_MENTION 211 (1.39%).")
ext("C058", " Report 59 (Tappsk): Russian-language acquisition — the founder's vc.ru article (MKT_PRESS 13), bloggers (MKT_BLOGGER 19: 'посмотрел видео у Маргулана'; 'я смотрела тик ток'), word of mouth (MKT_WOM 41), ads only 9.")
ext("C043", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_HABIT_OPTIONS 113 (0.74%) and REQ_RECURRENCE 51 — habit scheduling and count options are a steady request beside REQ_CUSTOMIZE 234, the largest single request (80 of the 4★ reviews).")
ext("C014", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_ADVANCE_REMINDER 68 — earlier or multiple reminders per task.")
ext("C015", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_SHARED 65 (0.43%) never stops across eight years; the listing advertises sharing a task to a friend's Tappsk, praised by only 5.")
ext("C045", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_PROJECTS 33, REQ_TAGS 24, REQ_CHECKLIST 21; PR_LISTS 185 and hidden lists (books, films, shopping) 29 are praised.")
ext("C046", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_INTEGRATIONS 57 (Siri, Reminders, Health), REQ_CALENDAR_SYNC 56, REQ_NOTIF_ACTIONS 28, REQ_QUICK_ACTIONS 21.")
ext("C108", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_GOALS 52 (4.73★).")
ext("C066", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_TIMER 43 (distinctive in Ukraine, 3.00×).")
ext("C017", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_PASSCODE 12 (4.92★).")
ext("C252", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_NOTIF_ACTIONS 28 — actions from the notification or lock screen; the listing's 'reminders that repeat until acted on' is praised (PR_REMINDERS 401).")
ext("C258", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the listing advertises reminders that repeat until acted on; PR_REMINDERS 401 (2.64%, 4.90★) is the fourth-largest praise theme and distinctive in SA, CA, AU and GB.")
ext("C037", " Report 59 (Tappsk): REQ_FAMILY_SHARE 13; 'написано, что поддерживается семейный доступ' (it says Family Sharing is supported) is a paid-twice complaint.")
ext("C064", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the monthly at ~300 ₽ is called too high — 'Месячную подписку можно было бы сделать хотя бы 150р, а не 300'; 'Люди куда охотнее отдадут 100р в месяц'; 'Рублей 199-299' — while the lifetime at 449–600 ₽ on sale (list 1,490–2,500 ₽) sells; MON_PRICE 252 (1.66%), distinctive in France (2.16×) and Turkey (4.49×).")
ext("C092", " Report 59 (Tappsk): the same lifetime unlock is named at 449 ₽ and 2,500 ₽ and at $14 / €4–10 within a year; regional prices could not be established from the corpus.")
ext("C212", " Report 59 (Tappsk): MON_REFUND 159 (1.05%, 1.94★) — refunds reported granted ('Все вернули! Оперативно') and refused ('техподдержка не видит причины возврата' — support sees no reason for a refund; 'I was rejected to refund of 20$ annual subscription').")
ext("C063", " Report 59 (Tappsk): a trial that needs a card is itself a barrier ('полная версия в пробном периоде требует привязки карты', 1★) and the immediate-charge trial is the 1★ engine ([[C109]]).")
ext("C180", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 'Предложение куда-то исчезло и желание купить пропало' (the offer vanished somewhere and so did the wish to buy, 2★); 'нажимаю на купит, а кнопка не активная' — time-boxed discounts that disappear lose the sale.")
ext("C181", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 'Пишите сразу, что ПО платное, а не встроенные покупки' — reviewers want the paid nature stated in the listing, not hidden as 'in-app purchases'.")
ext("C232", " Report 59 (Tappsk): 'После отмены подписки приложение каждый раз пытается списать с карты средства' (after cancelling, the app keeps trying to charge the card) — off-store billing retries after cancellation and after deletion; the fix is to stop retries after deletion.")

